<form autocomplete="off"><header><h1>{{actor.name}}</h1><p><strong>Kugutsu puppet</strong> · Medium · Source: Hijutsu Vol. 2, printed pp. 101–102</p></header>
<nav class="tabs puppet-tabs" data-group="primary"><a class="item" data-tab="overview">Overview</a><a class="item" data-tab="devices">Devices</a><a class="item" data-tab="rules">Puppet Rules</a></nav>
<section class="puppet-body">
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="overview"><label>Controller <select name="flags.shinobi-no-sho-revamp.puppetProfile.controllerId"><option value="">Not assigned</option>{{#each controllers}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
<p>Controller: {{controllerName}}. Attacks and defenses below read the controller’s current sheet.</p>{{#unless hasController}}<p>Assign a controller before play. The first assignment initializes Absorption from their Mechanics.</p>{{/unless}}{{#if disabled}}<p><strong>UNUSABLE — 0 Absorption. Requires repair.</strong></p>{{/if}}
<table><tr><th>Mechanics</th><td>{{stats.mechanics}}</td><th>Body Hardness</th><td>{{stats.hardness}}</td></tr><tr><th>Maximum Absorption</th><td>{{stats.absorptionMax}}</td><th>Remaining</th><td><input type="number" min="0" max="{{stats.absorptionMax}}" name="flags.shinobi-no-sho-revamp.puppetProfile.absorptionRemaining" value="{{remaining}}"></td></tr><tr><th>Attack (Ranged Combat)</th><td>{{stats.attack}}</td><th>Dodge / Anticipate</th><td>{{stats.dodge}} / {{stats.anticipate}}</td></tr><tr><th>Control range</th><td>{{stats.controlRange}} m</td><th>Device ranged reach</th><td>{{stats.attackRange}} m</td></tr></table>
<p><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="attack">Roll Attack</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="dodge">Roll Dodge</button><button type="button" class="puppet-roll" data-roll="anticipate">Roll Anticipate</button><button type="button" class="puppet-repair">Complete 4-hour Repair</button></p>
<p><strong>Example aptitudes:</strong> {{aptitudesText}}. These are the book’s sample purchases for this puppet. Allocate the controller’s power points and meet normal prerequisites; their bonuses are not automatically added to these rolls.</p><p><strong>Slots:</strong> 1 Light, 2 Standard, 1 Heavy. <strong>Material cost:</strong> {{puppet.materialsCost}} Ryo, including the 600 Ryo Medium skeleton. Creating an actor does not deduct money.</p></div>
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="devices"><button type="button" class="puppet-refill">Village Resupply — Restore Device Uses</button>{{#each devices}}<details open style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #999;margin:8px 0"><summary><strong>{{name}}</strong> — {{slot}}</summary>{{#if canAttack}}<p>Weapon Damage +{{weaponDamage}} · Base damage {{baseDamage}} = ceil(Mechanics / 2 + Weapon Damage).</p>{{/if}}{{#if limited}}<p>Remaining uses: {{remainingUses}} / {{maxUses}} <button type="button" class="puppet-use-charge" data-item-id="{{id}}">Spend One Use</button></p>{{/if}}{{#if minimumMechanics}}<p>Requires Mechanics {{minimumMechanics}}. {{#if locked}}<strong>Prerequisite not met.</strong>{{/if}}</p>{{/if}}<p style="white-space:pre-line">{{description}}</p></details>{{/each}}<p>Device activations normally use a Standard Action. Handle device-specific chakra, areas, poison, effects and aptitude modifiers manually; spending a use only updates its remaining charge.</p></div>
<div class="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="rules"><p>Puppets are constructed weapons, separate from animal Kuchiyose. Medium puppets have Body Hardness 1 and Absorption 5 × the controller’s Mechanics. At 0 Absorption they become unusable; a Tool Kit and 4-hour repair restores them. They do not use creature Vitality, NC allocation or half-Vitality rules.</p><p>Connecting chakra threads costs a Partial Action and 1 ordinary Chakra per puppet; control is sustained. Drawing a puppet is a Free Action. Base control range: 10m + 2m per Spirit; ranged device reach: 5m + Spirit. Transfer the controller’s Movement or Standard Action for puppet movement or attacks. Kurohigi determines how many puppets may be connected/acted with; creating actor copies does not increase that limit.</p><p>All attacks use the controller’s Ranged Combat, including melee maneuvers. Use the controller’s Dodge/Anticipate for defense. Apply their relevant condition penalties and camouflage. Manual skill checks for Agility/Dexterity tasks use the controller’s Sleight of Hand. The puppet must be visible to its controller.</p><p>Fear, fascination and fatigue do not affect the puppet as a human, but movement restrictions can. An uncontrolled puppet is a defenseless object. Rules for chakra threads, compatible aptitudes, control limits, winged targets, maneuvers and other Kugutsu features remain in force.</p><p>This sheet tracks Absorption and device uses, and rolls controller precision. It does not automatically pay thread/device chakra, enforce turn actions, install upgrades, place summoned tokens or apply damage. Drag this actor to a scene for a selectable token. The token hides ordinary character Vitality bars to avoid confusing them with puppet Absorption.</p></div>
</section></form>
